reference:
 The Io\Poll\Context class
 Io\Poll\Context




   &reftitle.intro;

    A polling context watches a set of handles and reports which of them are
    ready for reading or writing.
    It is the entry point of the polling API: handles are
    registered with Io\Poll\Context::add, and
    Io\Poll\Context::wait blocks until one of them is
    ready.


    The context relies on the polling mechanism of the operating system,
    represented by the Io\Poll\Backend enum.
    Unlike stream_select, the set of watched streams is
    kept between calls instead of being passed again on each of them.


    Objects of this class cannot be cloned or serialized.





